# **Every env file except `.env` itself** (XIV-56).
#
# A list was what went wrong here. `.env.test` was on it, `.env.dev` was not, so
# `.env.dev` shipped inside the production image — carrying
# `MAILER_DSN=smtp://mailpit:1025`, naming a service that does not exist there,
# and `APP_SECRET=dev-only-not-a-real-secret` beside it. Inert, because `.env.dev`
# is only read at `APP_ENV=dev` and production does not run that way, but it is
# the sort of thing somebody reads out of an image and believes. The list needed
# a line added every time a file was, and one day it did not get one.
#
# A pattern needs nothing remembered. `.env` stays because Symfony reads it for
# defaults and `composer dump-env prod` compiles from it; everything else is
# either a developer's machine or another environment, and neither is this
# image's business.
#
# `.env.local.php` is excluded here and *present in the image anyway*, which is
# correct and worth saying so nobody removes this line to "fix" it: the build
# generates its own with `composer dump-env prod` (see the Dockerfile). Excluding
# it from the context is what stops a stale one from somebody's laptop being
# copied over the top of the real one.
.env.*

# Composer credentials (XIV-99). `.gitignore` covers this file for git and Docker
# does not read `.gitignore` — the build context is a separate list, and this is
# the one that decides what reaches an image. Leaving it out put a real token
# into a production image: `COPY --link --exclude=frankenphp/ . ./` copies the
# context wholesale, and the file survived at mode 600 owned by root, where a
# grep run as the image's own unprivileged user could not see it.
#
# The credential reaches the build through a BuildKit secret mount instead, which
# exists only while `composer install` runs.
auth.json

# **The agents' worktrees, and every other directory that is somebody's machine**
# (XIV-96, and the same lesson `auth.json` above taught).
#
# `.claude/worktrees/` holds a full checkout per agent — thirty-three of them at
# the time this line was written, 5.7 GB — and `COPY --link --exclude=frankenphp/
# . ./` copies the context wholesale. So the customer-facing image, whose entire
# point is not containing the administration surface, contained thirty-three
# copies of it, nested one directory deeper than the verification looked. The
# image was 7.3 GB. Neither `git status` nor `bin/ci` could see it, because the
# worktrees are gitignored and the agent that wrote the check had none.
#
# **A pattern was tried here first and is not available.** `**/.*/` reads as
# "every hidden directory" and would have needed nothing remembered, which is
# what the `.env.*` note above argues for — but `.dockerignore` has no
# directory-only form, so it excluded `.env` as well and the build died in
# `composer dump-env prod`. Hence a list, and hence the whole-of-`/app` check in
# the Dockerfile: the list is what keeps the image small, and that check is what
# catches the entry this list does not have yet.
.claude/
.agents/
.idea/
.deptrac.cache/
.php-cs-fixer.cache/
.phpunit.cache/

# Coverage reports: somebody's last run rather than this build's. 67 MB at the
# time of writing.
coverage/
